<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <title><%= content_for(:title) || "Door" %></title>
    <%# Full-bleed in a browser; inside the app its bars keep the page in the safe area. %>
    <meta name="viewport" content="<%= native_viewport(cover: true) %>">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Coustard:wght@400;900&family=Inter:ital,opsz,wght@0,14..32,100..900;1,14..32,100..900&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.png" type="image/png">
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag :app, "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
    <%= javascript_importmap_tags %>
  </head>

  <%# The door on show night: a phone-first page with nothing in the way.
      The header (Tim, 2026-10-18) says what this is, "Work the door", and
      whose door: the organization's name, as a link to its box office, with
      the date and time. Never a person's picture: someone handing over money
      should see the organization, not a stranger's face. In the app the native
      bar holds the title and the way back, so the header is just the
      organization and the time. %>
  <%
    door_organization = @listing&.organization || @organization
    native = turbo_native_app?
  %>
  <body class="inter-regular text-slate-700 bg-gray-50">
    <%# The header is a little box (Tim, 2026-10-18): "Work the door", the
        organization's name under it (plain words, never a link: a link to the
        ticket page confused people), the date and time under that. Nothing
        shares a line, so nothing gets cut off on a phone. %>
    <%# The notch's room only in a browser: in the app its own bar is above
        the page, and Android's web view still reports the status bar here. %>
    <header class="<%= native ? '' : 'sticky top-0 z-10' %> bg-gray-50" style="<%= 'padding-top: env(safe-area-inset-top)' unless native %>">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pt-3">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white px-4 py-3">
          <%# The way back, a chevron beside the title (Tim, 2026-10-18): a
              show's page goes back to its organization's list; that list goes
              back to the choice of organizations when there are several. The
              app has its own. %>
          <% back_path = if native then nil
                         elsif @listing then door_index_path(organization: @listing.organization_id)
                         elsif @organization && @organizations&.many? then door_index_path
                         end %>
          <% if content_for?(:door_header) %>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2"><%= yield :door_header %></div>
          <% elsif !native %>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-1">
              <% if back_path %>
                <%= link_to back_path, class: "flex-shrink-0 p-1.5 -ml-2 rounded-lg text-gray-500 hover:text-gray-900 hover:bg-gray-100", "aria-label": (@listing ? "All the shows" : "All your organizations") do %>
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/></svg>
                <% end %>
              <% end %>
              <div class="coustard-regular text-xl leading-tight text-gray-900">Work the door</div>
            </div>
          <% end %>
          <% if door_organization %>
            <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-0.5"><%= door_organization.name %></div>
          <% end %>
          <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 tabular-nums mt-0.5"><%= Time.current.strftime("%A, %B %-d · %-l:%M %p") %></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>
    <main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pt-3 pb-5">
      <%= render partial: "shared/notice", locals: { notice: notice, alert: alert } %>
      <%= yield %>
    </main>
    <%= render "shared/native/bridge" %>
  </body>
</html>
